{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00009",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.16,
      "end_seconds": 8.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "Hi doctor, sorry, the lift was out and I had to take the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.59,
      "end_seconds": 13.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.19,
      "end_seconds": 25.57,
      "duration_seconds": 10.38,
      "text": "It's tightness in my chest when I walk, mostly. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 27.13,
      "end_seconds": 36.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse is 88 beats a minute, pressure 165 over 100, temperature 36.6, saturation 99 percent, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.97,
      "end_seconds": 44.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Okay, noted. When did you first notice it? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.75,
      "end_seconds": 49.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.53,
      "end_seconds": 53.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.99,
      "end_seconds": 62.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.74,
      "end_seconds": 69.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.98,
      "end_seconds": 74.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.82,
      "end_seconds": 79.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.23,
      "end_seconds": 86.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get breathlessness on exertion as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.06,
      "end_seconds": 92.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 92.79,
      "end_seconds": 99.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.65,
      "end_seconds": 104.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Have you had tiredness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.75,
      "end_seconds": 113.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "Yes, actually. Um, um, the breathlessness on exertion? That's been for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.53,
      "end_seconds": 124.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.86,
      "end_seconds": 134.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "A four out of ten, I suppose. Resting helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.73,
      "end_seconds": 139.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Did you get pain at rest or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.53,
      "end_seconds": 155.2,
      "duration_seconds": 13.67,
      "text": "No, um, no pain at rest, no fever. I was sweating with it at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.78,
      "end_seconds": 163.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "So, and what about swelling in the ankles, fainting, palpitations or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.1,
      "end_seconds": 171.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "No swelling in the ankles, fainting, palpitations or cough, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.62,
      "end_seconds": 175.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.23,
      "end_seconds": 178.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.98,
      "end_seconds": 182.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.13,
      "end_seconds": 185.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.76,
      "end_seconds": 190.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Is there anything medical in your background?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.49,
      "end_seconds": 198.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.07,
      "end_seconds": 200.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.05,
      "end_seconds": 210.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "I have diabetes, for nearly five years. I've had high cholesterol, yes. I've got heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.59,
      "end_seconds": 220.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "Right, so diabetes and high cholesterol are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.71,
      "end_seconds": 237.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Right, what medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.22,
      "end_seconds": 243.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Telmisartan, 40 milligrams, maybe, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.96,
      "end_seconds": 249.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Alright, did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.5,
      "end_seconds": 266.89,
      "duration_seconds": 15.39,
      "text": "No, it's at home. Glycomet. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day. Though honestly, some days I forget to take it. Aspirin. I take it 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 268.06,
      "end_seconds": 272.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 150 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.38,
      "end_seconds": 279.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.4,
      "end_seconds": 288.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "No, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.28,
      "end_seconds": 294.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.9,
      "end_seconds": 297.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "My mother has migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.0,
      "end_seconds": 313.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.46,
      "end_seconds": 318.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.33,
      "end_seconds": 320.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.43,
      "end_seconds": 326.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Yes, I had my tonsils out, when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.19,
      "end_seconds": 330.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.83,
      "end_seconds": 342.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "I don't drink at all. I walk for about half an hour most days. I try to avoid too much sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.62,
      "end_seconds": 348.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Let me examine, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.66,
      "end_seconds": 350.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.1,
      "end_seconds": 354.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Let me look at this properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.01,
      "end_seconds": 374.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Lungs are clear and there's no swelling in your ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.96,
      "end_seconds": 380.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.39,
      "end_seconds": 389.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmurs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.1,
      "end_seconds": 421.39,
      "duration_seconds": 28.29,
      "text": "That's all I need, thank you. Let me tell you where I've got to. My working impression is angina-type chest pain. It could also be a musculoskeletal cause, so we'll keep that open. I'd also keep gastro-oesophageal reflux in mind. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had tightness in your chest when you walk for about two weeks, severe, and no cough or pain at rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.7,
      "end_seconds": 426.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.2,
      "end_seconds": 431.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "I'm going to order an echocardiogram, for chest tightness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 431.76,
      "end_seconds": 434.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "The earliest is Friday, 10 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.79,
      "end_seconds": 440.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I'm going to order a lipid profile, for cardiovascular risk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 441.25,
      "end_seconds": 447.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "Doctor, I did an ECG before they came in, the result's on your screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.32,
      "end_seconds": 476.29,
      "duration_seconds": 26.97,
      "text": "Good, thank you. The treatment will be atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. You take it by mouth. That's for cardiovascular risk. For this, GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes, as needed. That should help with chest tightness. Don't push through the chest tightness, stop, sit down, and use the spray if I've given it to you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 477.35,
      "end_seconds": 509.22,
      "duration_seconds": 31.87,
      "text": "Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. A cardiologist would be the right next step, I'll refer you. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's hold off on a treadmill test for now, and if there's no change in two weeks we can revisit it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 511.21,
      "end_seconds": 519.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "Do get help quickly if the chest tightness comes at rest or lasts more than fifteen minutes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 520.92,
      "end_seconds": 521.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 522.42,
      "end_seconds": 525.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 526.9,
      "end_seconds": 530.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, you know, thanks."
    }
  ]
}